# tfpp-ds41: this node's own values (bash, sourced by start_stage.sh / stop_stage.sh). Copy to node.env on each N1X
# and keep exactly ONE block. Keys: ROLE LAYERS LISTEN DOWN MODEL_DIR ENGRAM_DIR TOKEN_MAP BUDGET_GIB RESERVE_GIB TRACE
# BENCH ORACLE EXPERTS GPU_GUARD_PORTS ALLOW_GPU_SHARING VERIFY_SHARDS TFPP_WARM_MS TFPP_DS41_VENV TFPP_DS41_TF_ROOT
# TF_API_KEY_FILE (the last: the leader only; never printed, never digested).
# USB4: the 64 GB node = 10.77.0.1, the 128 GB node = 10.77.0.2. Each inbound hop reaches WSL through
# scripts/glm/relay_hop.ps1 on the receiving node's Windows side (unchanged, it takes any address and ports):
#   powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File relay_hop.ps1 -ListenAddress <that node's 10.77.0.x> -Ports 5321
# Start the stages in any order (a follower retries until the next stage answers LINK); stop the leader only.
# Engram: each owner gets a folder holding exactly the tables of the layers it owns (the fork globs the folder).
# Stages sharing one GPU (T1-3 on the 128 GB node) need BUDGET_GIB each and ALLOW_GPU_SHARING=1; at CAP the leader also
# sums their weights + needs on that GPU (capacity.check_caps), so lower TFPP_DS41_WORKSPACE_GIB (default 4) when it
# refuses. Each stage keeps its pid / log in its own folder ($TFPP_DS41_STATE/<role>-<A>-<B>).
# Other GPU servers on this node: list their ports, and start_stage.sh
# refuses to start while one listens (they share the GPU's memory; CAP measures it once):
#   GPU_GUARD_PORTS="18891 <port> <port>"    # default 18891 (a tfpp-ds41 leader's HTTP)
# Any TFPP_* / TF_DS_* / TF_EXL3_* / TENSORFOLD_* line here is exported to the stage (TFPP_DS41_WORKSPACE_GIB=2.5,
# TFPP_FAULT=leader:after-step:3, TFPP_DS41_ALLOW_TRITON=1, TF_DS_ENGRAM_THREADS=...); the digested ones must match on
# every stage (HELLO). CONTEXT / PARALLEL / MTP_DRAFTS / HTTP_PORT given on start_stage.sh's command line beat cluster.env's.
# A drafting leader that holds no layer 0 can do without shard 1 (6.5 GB): `python -m tfpp.ds41.testmodel extract
# <shard-1> embed.weight $MODEL_DIR/embed.weight.safetensors` and leave shard 1 out of its MODEL_DIR (the preflight takes
# the file for the shard; both together are refused).
# The paths below assume the checkout at ~/hive-ram and the fork's sources at ~/tf-dsv41: edit them to yours.

# ==== T1-c6 (spec 15.6, the main test): S11 [0,6) on the 128 GB node -> [6,11) on the 64 GB node (leader) ==========
# -- the 128 GB node: stage 0, owns Engram L1 and L4 --
ROLE=follower
LAYERS=0:6
MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/ds41-s11              # make_testmodel.sh's output (the same on both nodes)
ENGRAM_DIR=$HOME/engram-d/both               # t1.safetensors + t4.safetensors (Mode D, made on this node)
DOWN=10.77.0.1:5321                          # the 64 GB node's relay (relay_hop.ps1 -ListenAddress 10.77.0.1 -Ports 5321)
RESERVE_GIB=3
TFPP_WARM_MS=1.0
TFPP_DS41_TF_ROOT=$HOME/tf-dsv41/src
TRACE=$HOME/tfpp-ds41-tests/c6.s0.jsonl
# -- the 64 GB node: the leader --
# ROLE=leader
# LAYERS=6:11
# MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/ds41-s11
# LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5321
# RESERVE_GIB=2.5
# TFPP_WARM_MS=1.0
# TFPP_DS41_TF_ROOT=$HOME/tf-dsv41/src
# CONTEXT=8192                               # the test's (cluster.env's 262144 is production's); PARALLEL=2
# PARALLEL=2
# BENCH=$HOME/hive-ram/tfpp/tfpp/ds41/bench_prompts.jsonl   # no HTTP; QUIT ends the chain afterwards
# TRACE=$HOME/tfpp-ds41-tests/c6.jsonl       # compare with the 128 GB node's T-ref trace (python -m tfpp.ds41.compare)
# The 64 GB node short of budget for the leader? swap the roles: the 64 GB node [0,6) (ENGRAM_DIR both), the 128 GB node
# leader [6,11).

# ==== T1-c3: S11 [0,3) on the 64 GB node -> [3,11) on the 128 GB node (leader; non-stage-0 Engram owner, stretch cut) ==
# -- the 64 GB node: stage 0, owns Engram L1 --
# ROLE=follower
# LAYERS=0:3
# MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/ds41-s11
# ENGRAM_DIR=$HOME/engram-d/L1
# DOWN=10.77.0.2:5321                        # the 128 GB node's relay
# RESERVE_GIB=2.5
# -- the 128 GB node: the leader, owns Engram L4 --
# ROLE=leader
# LAYERS=3:11
# MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/ds41-s11
# ENGRAM_DIR=$HOME/engram-d/L4
# LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5321
# CONTEXT=8192
# PARALLEL=2
# BENCH=$HOME/hive-ram/tfpp/tfpp/ds41/bench_prompts.jsonl
# TRACE=$HOME/tfpp-ds41-tests/c3.jsonl

# ==== T1-3: 128 GB node [0,3) -> 64 GB node [3,6) -> 128 GB node [6,11) (two hops; the middle stage owns the replay
# layer) ==========
# 128 GB node, stage 0: ROLE=follower LAYERS=0:3 ENGRAM_DIR=$HOME/engram-d/L1 DOWN=10.77.0.1:5321 BUDGET_GIB=20
#                       ALLOW_GPU_SHARING=1 (a second node.env folder: TFPP_DS41_CONF=... start_stage.sh)
# 64 GB node, middle:   ROLE=follower LAYERS=3:6 ENGRAM_DIR=$HOME/engram-d/L4 LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5321 DOWN=10.77.0.2:5322
# 128 GB node, leader:  ROLE=leader LAYERS=6:11 LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5322 BUDGET_GIB=40 ALLOW_GPU_SHARING=1 CONTEXT=8192
#                       PARALLEL=2 BENCH=... TRACE=...
# (relays: the 64 GB node -ListenAddress 10.77.0.1 -Ports 5321; the 128 GB node -ListenAddress 10.77.0.2 -Ports 5322)

# ==== T-X0: the same reference on both nodes (S11 with 16 experts a layer): run_shortened.sh T-X0 on each, then
# python -m tfpp.ds41.compare nodeA/TX0.jsonl nodeB/TX0.jsonl (EXPERTS=16)

# ==== production (v2, three nodes, spec 16.1): plan fit decides the cuts; e.g. P1 (17, 25) ==========================
# a third node:     ROLE=follower LAYERS=0:17 MODEL_DIR=$HOME/models/ds41 ENGRAM_DIR=$HOME/engram/both DOWN=<64gb-node>:5321
# the 64 GB node:   ROLE=follower LAYERS=17:25 LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5321 DOWN=10.77.0.2:5322
# the 128 GB node:  ROLE=leader LAYERS=25:40 LISTEN=0.0.0.0:5322 TF_API_KEY_FILE=$HOME/.config/tfpp-ds41/api_key
#                   (CONTEXT / PARALLEL / MTP_DRAFTS / SERVED_NAME / HTTP_PORT from cluster.env; the key file closes
#                   every route but /health, which matters with cluster.env's HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0)

# ---- any node, optional ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TOKEN_MAP=$HOME/.cache/dsv41_token_map.json  # the Engram owners' token map cache (TF_DS_TOKEN_MAP)
# EXPERTS=16                                   # T-X0's proxy only: the first 16 experts a layer (every stage alike)
# ORACLE=$HOME/tfpp-ds41-tests/serial.json     # T1-oracle: a serial reference run's --bench-out (the leader)
# VERIFY_SHARDS=1                              # check this stage's shards against their Hub sha256 first (cached)
# GPU_GUARD_PORTS="18891 <port>"               # other GPU servers on this node (see the top)
# TFPP_DS41_VENV=$HOME/tf-venv-dsv41
